From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Storage Maintainers <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] storage: Defer strict recovery writes

Applications must recognize an existing namespace before recovery can
change its files. Normal recovery can truncate a damaged journal or
remove incomplete keyspaces before that application check runs.

Add opt-in existing-only recovery with an explicit validation finish.
Inspect checksummed journal batches without trimming, permit only
zero padding between complete batches, and bound record and pending
batch allocations. Bound total physical journal bytes and fragment
inventory before decoding or scanning padding. Reject Clear records in
this mode instead of performing a persistent replay. Preserve files
and defer background maintenance and supported mutation APIs until
the application finishes validation.

After validation, trim verified padding before append writes resume and
start normal maintenance. Ordinary database recovery remains unchanged.

---
